{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevHbRiDhhTWtNrDQUht4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. I've completed my analysis. Here's my summary:\n\n**Requirement, restated in one sentence:**\nAdd a POST endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` to transition a shipment from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED` status, with idempotent retry behavior for already-confirmed shipments, rejection with HTTP 409 for cancelled shipments, HTTP 404 for non-existent shipments, and error responses consistent with the existing API.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:9-14` — Entity with status enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` — In-memory repository with save/findById/existsById\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-44` — POST /shipments creates with status CREATED\n- `ShipmentController.kt:46-52` — GET /shipments/{id} throws ResourceNotFoundException(404)\n- `ShipmentController.kt:20-24` — POST /shipments throws ConflictException(409) for duplicates\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:19-24` — ResourceNotFoundException and ConflictException classes\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum defines SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt` — Centralizes all error response formatting\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses; handler converts them to `ApiError` envelope\n- State-change operations return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(entity)`\n- 404 uses `ResourceNotFoundException(ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message)`\n- 409 uses `ConflictException(ErrorCode.code, message)`\n- Tests use MockMvc with `jsonPath(\"$.error.code\")` to verify error codes\n- @BeforeEach with `repository.clear()` to reset state between tests\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — Add error code for invalid shipment state (cancellation blocks confirmation) — **necessary for requirement's 409 response**\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add `@PostMapping` confirm endpoint — **core requirement**\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add tests for all four cases (CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotent, CANCELLED rejected, 404) — **required by test criterion**\n\n**Risks:**\n- ErrorCode enum is client-facing API; adding one must be intentional\n- Idempotent retry (already-confirmed succeeds) requires defensive logic\n- CANCELLED is write-only via test fixture; confirm must handle it correctly\n\n**Open questions:**\n- Which error code for cancelled shipment? Ticket says 409 but doesn't name it. I'll add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` (covers cancellation and future invalid states).\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to ErrorCode enum after SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS. Describes when a shipment cannot be confirmed due to its current state (e.g., already cancelled).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add new endpoint:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment\n   ```\n   Logic: \n   - Fetch shipment or throw `ResourceNotFoundException(ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, ...)`\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw `ConflictException(ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, \"Cannot confirm a cancelled shipment\")`\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED and save\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent) — no error, no change\n   - Return the shipment (updated or unchanged)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test methods:\n   - `confirm_CREATED_to_CONFIRMED` — create shipment, confirm it, verify status changed to CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm_idempotent_already_CONFIRMED` — confirm same shipment twice, both succeed, status stays CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm_CANCELLED_rejected_409` — insert CANCELLED shipment directly to repo, confirm fails with 409 and SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - `confirm_not_found_404` — confirm non-existent ID, fails with 404 and SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Could have used existing error code (e.g., SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS) for cancelled shipment, but that's semantically wrong—already-exists refers to duplicate IDs, not invalid state. Adding a new code is more maintainable and consistent with error taxonomy.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Write | Output | Through |\n|------|-------|------|-------|--------|---------|\n| CREATED→CONFIRMED | shipmentId=S-1 | findById | save(status=CONFIRMED) | 200 + Shipment(status=CONFIRMED) | response body |\n| Idempotent retry | shipmentId=S-1 (already CONFIRMED) | findById | none | 200 + Shipment(status=CONFIRMED) | response body |\n| CANCELLED | shipmentId=S-2 (CANCELLED) | findById | none | 409 ApiError(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE) | GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| Not found | shipmentId=unknown | none | none | 404 ApiError(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) | GlobalExceptionHandler |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- All four tests use `post(\"/shipments/{id}/confirm\")` with the new endpoint\n- CREATED test creates fresh shipment, confirms, checks status changed\n- Idempotent test confirms twice, verifies both return same status and second changes nothing\n- Cancelled test directly inserts CANCELLED shipment to repo (circumventing validation), confirms, verifies 409\n- Not-found test confirms non-existent ID, verifies 404\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. First, let me add the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3134,"cache_read_input_tokens":14876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3134},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b571ea9b-3215-446f-9728-9537c3339907","uuid":"aa69e92d-d890-4370-9c59-472d31727829",